# (BASIC 2.0) pictures on the text shell: sh tests/shots.sh EMU SD basic2s SECONDS T1 ...
# (BAS2SHOTS in the Makefile; REV $0B only):
#   1  SPRITES.BAS: balls (sprites from text art) bouncing in the graphics window
#   2  Esc: "Break in ...", the sprites gone, the window's picture stays
#   3  DRIFT.BAS (full screen 320 x 180): its title
#   4  Space starts it; the boat moved right and down, sprites on the river
#   5  Esc: back to the desktop, the graphics window shows the last picture
#   6  SCROLLER.BAS: full screen over a 640 x 360 world, the panel at the top, raster bands
#   7  Alt+Tab: the desktop, the program still running (its window shows the top left)
#   8  Esc (the console has the focus): Break, the BASIC window as it was
#   9  CONT: the full screen again, scrolled on
#  10  Esc, SCREEN 0: the window closed, the console alone
1500 {esc}
+1500 basic -r /programs/SPRITES.BAS\n
+5000 {esc}
+1500 run /programs/drift.bas\n
+4500 {d2C}
+200 {u2C}
+800 {d4F}{d51}
+1500 {u4F}{u51}
+1500 {esc}
+1500 run /programs/scroller.bas\n
+7500 {dE2}
+100 {d2B}
+100 {u2B}
+100 {uE2}
+2000 {esc}
+1500 cont\n
+2500 {esc}
+1000 screen 0\n
